cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Bidirectional cross-attention does not perform cross-modal interaction:
  architectural degeneracy and variance decomposition in histopathology-clinical
  data fusion
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Tomasz
    family-names: Pruś
    email: prus.tomasz.1972@gmail.com
    affiliation: Independent Researcher
    city: Łódź
    country: PL
license: MIT
keywords:
  - multimodal fusion
  - cross-attention
  - computational pathology
  - reproducibility
  - variance decomposition
  - TCGA-BRCA
abstract: >-
  Code accompanying a study showing that one direction of bidirectional
  cross-attention between whole-slide images and a clinical feature vector is
  mathematically degenerate, that late fusion outperforms early fusion on
  weakly correlated modalities, and that at cohort sizes typical of digital
  pathology, weight-initialisation variance exceeds architectural differences
  by a factor of five.
